  "articleBody": "Starting a basement finishing project is exciting, but nothing sours the mood faster than unexpected hidden costs. To keep your budget on track and avoid those unwelcome surprises, it's smart to be proactive and informed. One of the biggest pitfalls is not fully addressing moisture problems *before* you start. If you skip this, you could face costly repairs down the line for mold, rot, or damaged finishes. Always ensure your contractor assesses for dampness and includes any necessary waterproofing in the initial quote. Another common mistake is accepting vague bids. A detailed bid should spell out exactly what's included – from materials and labor to who's responsible for pulling permits. Without this clarity, you might find yourself paying extra for things you assumed were covered. Also, don't overlook code requirements. Features like egress windows, proper ventilation, and electrical upgrades often trigger permit needs and add to the project cost. Make sure your contractor clarifies all regulatory considerations upfront. By focusing on these points and working with a transparent contractor like HH Remodeling LLC, who serves areas from Aurora to Colorado Springs, you can head off those budget-busting surprises and enjoy a smoother finishing process.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}